 75AS2 H CUT=30-Jun-2013$                                                       
 75AS c  1976Sc13: E=23 MeV; magnetic spectrograph with FWHM=6 keV below        
 75AS2c  1100 keV and multigap magnetic spectrograph with FWHM                  
 75AS3c  |?30 keV above 1100 keV. Cross section uncertainties |?15%;            
 75AS4c  enriched targets; measured |s(|q). DWBA calculations                   
 75AS c  1974Be54, 1971Be30: E=17 MeV; multiangle spectrograph with             
 75AS2c  FWHM|?18-24 keV. Cross section uncertainty |?10%;                      
 75AS3c  enriched target; measured |s(|q). DWBA calculations.                   
 75AS c  2009Ka06 (also 2008KaZT): E=73 MeV beam provided by the AVF cyclotron  
 75AS2c  at RCNP, Osaka. Enriched target. The outgoing deuterons were           
 75AS3c  detected with Grand Raiden magnetic spectrometer, with an angular      
 75AS4c  aperture of |+1.1|'. FWHM=18 keV. Measured precise absolute cross      
 75AS5c  sections and relative cross sections where these are maximum for the   
 75AS6c  relevant L transfer, angular distributions. Spectroscopic factors      
 75AS7c  deduced from DWBA analysis using PTOLEMY code and six different sets   
 75AS8c  of optical-model potential parameters and two bound-state potential    
 75AS9c  parameters. Differences in (2J+1)C{+2}S values were less than 10%      
 75ASac  for different sets of used parameters. Polarized deuteron beam is      
 75ASbc  also used to obtain asymmetries and subsequent information about       
 75AScc  parities of levels. Uncertainty in cross sections: statistical         
 75ASdc  uncertainty of 1% for strong peaks; systematic uncertainties of 5%     
 75ASec  in absolute values and 3% in relative values. Multiplets have larger   
 75ASfc  uncertainties.                                                         
